window.docContents[145].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Placed/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Placed":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process › Placed.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 4 headline theorems depend on it 34 of 99 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nPlaced Libraries in Linked ELF Executables (Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.InElf)* Layer / Role: Arm64 Trusted Computing Base (Role::Spec, definitions only, 0 theorems).* Purpose & Key Exports: When a parsed static ELF executable contains a placed library (Obj.PlacedLib.InElf img lib pl): the patched text and data bytes of lib under placement pl are mapped in img's PT_LOAD segments (text executable, data readable, writable data writable), and each exported function has exactly one .symtab entry, at its placed address. Obj.PlacedLib.LinkedAt lib elfBytes pl says the raw ELF file elfBytes parses to such an image for the Placeable placement pl, and Obj.PlacedLib.LinkedIn lib elfBytes (∃ pl, LinkedAt) is the satisfiability (non-vacuity) witness for a layout-generic library contract (Obj.PlacedLib.subroutineOk) against a real linked binary. InElf constrains pl.ρ only through relocated text/data bytes and data-object placement: a spec mentioning pl.ρ x for a symbol no relocation or data object uses is not tied to the ELF's .symtab.* When to read: Read when auditing a library's precondition-satisfiability statement or when composing a library contract into a whole-binary ELF proof.\n\n\n\ndef ElfMapsL40–46 ↗#img maps bytes at [addr, addr + bytes.length) in its PT_LOAD segments: byte i is the byte at addr + i of the first segment containing that address (as in ElfImage.loadState), with a permission satisfying ok.\n\n3 declarations not shown (lines 48–67): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesArm64.Obj.PlacedLib.InElf.data, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.InElf.exports, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.InElf, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.InElf.text, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.LinkedAt, Arm64.Obj.PlacedLib.LinkedIn\n\nstructure MultiPlacedLib.InElfL69–85 ↗#The parsed executable img contains multi-block library lib placed under mpl:* every block i's patched text (lib.blocks[i].patched (lib.blockPlacement mpl i)) is mapped executable (r-x) at mpl.base i;* each data object's initial bytes (lib.patchedData mpl d) are mapped at mpl.ρ d.sym, readable if d.readOnly and exactly rw- otherwise;* each exported function e of lib is defined in some block i at offset off and its raw name lib.elfSym e has exactly one .symtab entry, at mpl.base i + off.\n\ndef MultiPlacedLib.LinkedAtL87–92 ↗#The ELF executable elfBytes links multi-block library lib at multi-block placement mpl: it parses (ElfImage.parse) to an image containing lib under mpl, and lib is Placeable at mpl.\n\nabbrev MultiPlacedLib.LinkedInL94–100 ↗#The ELF executable elfBytes links multi-block library lib at some multi-block placement (MultiPlacedLib.LinkedAt).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Process/Placed.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Process.Placed/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Process___Placed"}});